## Q2: Why do some countries have low margin?



**Key finding:** All underperforming countries share
one root cause — COGS represents 49–53% of gross sales.
Logistics and marketing are secondary issues.

**Auto-diagnosis result:**
- COGS-heavy countries - renegotiate supplier contracts
- Logistics-heavy countries -review delivery partners
- Marketing-heavy countries  -audit campaign ROI

**Recommendation:** Country-level action depends on
which cost driver dominates — the query identifies
this automatically per country.

## Q3: Which large orders are secretly loss-making?



| Risk Group | Share | Avg Margin | Key Pattern |
|------------|-------|------------|-------------|
| Loss-making | 2.1% | −6.34% | Wholesale + Flash Discount |
| Risky margin | 32.9% | 4–11% | All channels affected |
| Normal | 65% | 20%+ | Healthy baseline |

**Key insight:** Loss-making orders appear across ALL
revenue ranges ($500–$10K). A large gross sales figure
does not protect against losses — discounts and
logistics costs erode margin regardless of order size.

**Most dangerous combination:**
Wholesale channel + Flash Discount promotion
- highest concentration of loss-making orders.

**Recommendation:** Set minimum 12% margin floor
for all promotional orders above $500.
Review Flash Discount mechanics in Wholesale channel.

